# 🔷 SVG Logo Maker

A Node.js command-line tool that generates a custom SVG logo file from user input. Answer three prompts — text, text color, shape, and shape color — and the app writes a 300×200 `logo.svg` file instantly. Includes a Jest test suite for the shape classes.

---

## 📖 Overview

This project demonstrates object-oriented JavaScript in a CLI context. Three shape classes (`Circle`, `Triangle`, `Square`) each extend a base `Shape` class and implement a `render()` method that returns the SVG markup for that shape. Inquirer handles the prompts and the result is written to disk with Node's `fs` module.

---

## ✨ Features

- 🔤 Up to 3 characters of custom text rendered inside the shape
- 🎨 Text color and shape color — accepts any valid CSS color name or hex value
- ⭕ Three shape options: **Circle**, **Triangle**, **Square**
- 💾 Outputs `logo.svg` (300×200 pixels) to the project root
- ✅ Jest unit tests for all three shape classes

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|-----------|
| Runtime | Node.js |
| CLI Prompts | Inquirer v8.2.4 |
| Testing | Jest |
| Output | SVG (generated file) |

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- Node.js (v18+)

### Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Voobane/SVG-Logo-Maker.git
cd SVG-Logo-Maker
npm install
```

### Running the App

```bash
node index.js
```

Follow the prompts. When finished, open `logo.svg` in a browser or any SVG viewer.

### Running Tests

```bash
npx jest ./lib/shapes.test.js
```

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```
SVG-Logo-Maker/
├── lib/
│   ├── shapes.js        # Circle, Triangle, Square classes
│   └── shapes.test.js   # Jest unit tests
├── examples/            # Sample generated SVG output
├── index.js             # CLI entry point (Inquirer prompts + fs.writeFile)
├── package.json
└── README.md
```

---

## 💡 What I Learned

- Applying **OOP principles** — inheritance, base classes, and method overriding — in JavaScript
- Building a **CLI tool** with Inquirer's prompt chain
- Writing **SVG markup programmatically** from class `render()` methods
- Writing **Jest unit tests** to verify shape output without running the full CLI
- Using `fs.writeFile` to generate files from Node.js

---

## 📸 Example Output

> A blue circle with white "MSS" text:

```svg
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="300" height="200">
  <circle cx="150" cy="100" r="80" fill="blue" />
  <text x="150" y="115" text-anchor="middle" font-size="40" fill="white">MSS</text>
</svg>
```

